    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "FIRST FLIGHT\nAIRLINES\nLOCKHEED\nPROP-JET ELECTRA\nwith GM JET POWER\nAllison 501 Prop-Jet Engines and\nAeroproducts 606 Turbo-Propellers\nEAPP26-\n8.30 AM\n19:59\nU.S.ATR\nMALLY\nAIRP\nALASKA STATEHOOD • IC\nAir mail\nCol. J. H. Lackey, Jr.\nAEGIN IB TU SLOG\nRM4B137, Pentagon\nWashington 25, D3 C.",
      "43117801\nMAIL SERVICE\n• 4 MAY 1959\n0\n6961-\nWdocol\nKOLONIE\n2012,149.2014a",
      "This first flight cachet commemorates the first fight of the four-engine\nLockheed Electra luxuryliner on routes of National Airlines. This is another\nin a series of cachets being made available as major world airlines phase into\ncommercial service the 450-mph transports, with the General Motors Jet Power\nteam of Allison Model 501-D13 Prop-jet engines and Aeroproducts 606 Turbo-\npropellers.\nVice-President of General Motors\nGeneral Manager of Allison Division",
      "22.149.2014L"
